Fixes #502  .

Changes proposed in this PR:

- update unit tests for example config to verify the block confirmations value;
- update the marketplace flow README to use ExampleConfig;
- remove the tweak from the `wait_for_transaction_receipt_and_block_confirmations` function;
- remove duplicates of python word from the marketplace flow README.

## Summary
<!-- Implementation and architectural changes introduced. -->

Axios has a number of issues both opened and closed relating to file uploads and streams in general. I read through each one and tried a number of things, including setting [`maxRedirects: 0` to prevent streams from being pulled into memory](https://github.com/axios/axios/issues/1045) and [setting a dummy `transformRequest` that just returned the data untransformed](https://github.com/axios/axios/issues/1250). I tried this with and without streams, uploading 175 files of varying sizes (from 19kb to 10MB). Each resulting in a small minority of files uploaded with different sizes than they are known to have.

Adding the `Content-Length` header doesn't work for streams, [as this issue suggests it might](https://github.com/axios/axios/issues/961). However, using `readFileSync` along with `Content-Length` seems to be the secret incantation that solves the problem. Using this combination, I've uploaded 3,325 files without issue.

## Test Plan
<!-- How to test changes. -->

Here's my test script,

```typescript
import assert from 'assert';
import { lstatSync, readdirSync, readFileSync, statSync } from 'fs';
import { join } from 'path';

import { logError, uploadFile, VertexClient, VertexError } from './index';

void main();

async function main(): Promise<void> {
  try {
    const client = await VertexClient.build({
      client: { id: '', secret: '' },
      basePath: 'https://platform.platdev.vertexvis.io',
    });

    const dir = '/Users/rocky.warren/Documents/test-files';
    const files = readdirSync(dir)
      .map((fileOrDir) => ({ name: fileOrDir, path: join(dir, fileOrDir) }))
      .filter(({ path }) => lstatSync(path).isFile());
    assert(files.length === 175);

    const res = await Promise.all(
      files.map(({ name, path }) =>
        uploadFile({
          client,
          createFileReq: { data: { attributes: { name }, type: 'file' } },
          file: { data: readFileSync(path), size: statSync(path).size },
          verbose: true,
        })
      )
    );
    console.log(res[0].id);
  } catch (error) {
    logError(error as VertexError);
  }
}
```

And the script used to generate the files,

```bash
#!/usr/bin/env bash

# Public: Generate random files
#
# $1 - File size.
# $2 - Output directory.
# $3 - Number of files (default: 50).
#
# Returns nothing.
generate() {
  for ((i=0; i<${3:-50}; i++)); do
    head -c "$1" /dev/urandom > "$2/$1-$i.txt"
  done
}

main() {
  local dir=~/Documents/test-files
  mkdir $dir

  generate 10485760 $dir
  generate 1048576 $dir
  generate 57201 $dir
  generate 38134 $dir
  generate 19067 $dir
}

main
```

